    [Revert] Revert "[BugFix][KV Cache] Propagate resolved prefix retention config" (#17480) (#18029)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Reverts vllm-project/vllm-ascend#17480 (merge commit `6f8c631cc`).
    
    That change made the Ascend-owned KV cache paths consume the resolved
    `CacheConfig` / `KVCacheConfig.prefix_cache_retention_interval` field
    instead of reading `VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL` from
    `vllm.envs`. This PR restores the previous behavior in:
    
    - `KVPoolScheduler`
    - `KVPoolWorker._build_cache_coordinator`
    - `AscendHybridKVCacheCoordinator`
    - the GLM-Next custom `KVCacheConfig` planner
    
    This is a straight `git revert` of the squash-merged commit; no other
    logic is changed.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes — it restores the pre-#17480 behavior of these paths.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `git revert 6f8c631cc` applied on top of latest `main` (`a50eb57f1`).
    - One conflict in
    `tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_pool_worker.py`, where a later
    commit had added the adjacent `config.cache_config.prefix_match_unit =
    prefix_match_unit` line. Resolved by keeping `prefix_match_unit` and
    dropping only the reverted line.
    - Diff is the exact inverse of #17480: 10 files changed, 15
    insertions(+), 98 deletions(-).
    
